{"agent":"bfix-lane1","data":{"body":"Fixes bug B6159671e9b: The ci gate's command is `ddflow ci run`, not pytest, and its failed_tests list is capped (failed_tests_more=42 of 218 failures), so gate_baseline.apply/baseline_red.candidate_ids return no ids: a ci red only from failures that also fail on main ends `failed`, never `partial` baseline-red, and then unit_tests refuses to start (needs_ci). Observed on DX-baseline-red-auto-accept: ci 218 failed, all of the 42 listed except test_lookup_latency_budget also fail on a clean checkout of main. Fix: for the ci gate measure from the full failing-id list (junit/pytest report, not the capped tail) and run those ids on the base with the unit_tests command. Found on DX-baseline-red-auto-accept.\n\nWrite the regression test first and watch it FAIL on the unfixed code; then `ddflow complete fix-B6159671e9b --regression-test <test>` closes the bug with the task (or `ddflow bug fixed B6159671e9b --regression-test <test>` first).\n\nNot attached, they match nothing in the tree: ddflow/services/gates/baseline.py, ddflow/api/gate_baseline_notice.py, ddflow/templates/upgrade/unreleased/knob_added.gates.baseline_*.toml, tests/test_baseline_red_auto.py.","fixes":["B6159671e9b"],"globs":["ddflow/services/gate_accept.py","ddflow/services/gates/baseline_red.py","ddflow/services/gates/outcomes.py","ddflow/services/approvals/policy.py","ddflow/services/approvals/audit.py","ddflow/config_sections/gates.py","ddflow/api/gate_baseline.py","ddflow/api/gates/_run.py","ddflow/services/completion/rules.py","ddflow/services/testscope.py","ddflow/services/verify.py","README.md","tests/golden/__snapshots__/test_golden_outputs.ambr","tests/test_accept_partial_gate.py","ddflow/services/gates/__init__.py","ddflow/api/cirun.py","ddflow/surfaces/commands/ci.py"],"line":"","needs":[],"parent":"bugs-2","priority":8,"tags":["bugfix"],"title":"Fix bug B6159671e9b: ci gate can never be measured baseline-red"},"id":"ecd19de2ce08345ad78d6ae50","kind":"task.a