{"agent":"bfix-lane1","data":{"by":"Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"The new table assertion can pass vacuously. It slices `inspect.getsource(MC)` from the first occurrence of `RESOURCES: tuple` to the first occurrence of `RESOURCE_BY_URI`, but it never checks that the end marker is after the start marker or that the resulting slice is non-empty. For example, if `_core.py` contains `RESOURCE_BY_URI` in a module docstring, comment, or forward annotation before the actual `RESOURCES` tuple, then `start > end`, `table` becomes `\"\"`, and `assert \"fold(\" not in table and \"EventLog\" not in table` passes even if the real resource table contains `fold(` or `EventLog`. It also no longer checks the `RESOURCE_BY_URI` mapping line itself or any code between that line and `class Server`, so a violation such as `RESOURCE_BY_URI = {r.uri: r for r in RESOURCES if not fold(r)}` would be missed.","digest":"42cf60a84265a14e","location":"tests/test_roborev_findings.py::test_every_mcp_resource_is_served_through_the_cli","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_roborev_findings.py::test_every_mcp_resource_is_served_through_the_cli"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"The added comment asserts that monkeypatching `ddflow.infra.log.install_kind` now reaches the same name that both `upgrade_remedy` and `skew_message` call, but the diff only inserts the call-time `from . import install_kind` inside `upgrade_remedy`. `skew_message` in the same module is not changed, so it still calls the `install_kind` object bound at import time. A caller or regression test that monkeypatches `ddflow.infra.log.install_kind` and then invokes `ddflow.infra.log.skew_message(...)` will still observe the pre-patch install kind, so the pre-split behavior remains broken for one of the two promised functions.","digest":"2780e09fd6470374","location":"ddflow/infra/log/_skew.py:41","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/infra/log/_skew.py:41"}],"chunks_total":1,"combined_gates":["rubb